 "result": "Methods of `Config` in `src/tessel/config.py` (a `dict` subclass):\n\n- `__init__`: creates the config from an optional defaults dict and stores `root_path` for resolving relative file names.\n- `from_envvar`: loads a config file whose path is in the named environment variable, raising if it's unset unless `silent=True`.\n- `load_env_prefixed`: loads `TESSEL_*` environment variables (prefix stripped, values parsed with `json.loads` by default) and supports nested keys via `__`.\n- `from_pyfile`: executes a Python file and copies its uppercase names into the config, with optional silent failure for a missing file.\n- `from_object`: copies the uppercase attributes of an object or import-string module/class into the config.\n- `from_file`: reads a file with a caller-supplied `load` function (such as `json.load` or `tomllib.load`) and passes the result to `from_mapping`.\n- `from_mapping`: updates the config from a mapping and/or keyword arguments, keeping only uppercase keys, and always returns `True`.\n- `get_namespace`: returns a dict of the options starting with a given prefix, with the prefix trimmed and keys lowercased by default.\n- `__repr__`: returns `<Config {...}>`.\n\nThe same file also defines `ConfigAttribute`, a descriptor that forwards an app attribute to `app.config[name]`, with `__init__`, `__get__` and `__set__`. It isn't part of `Config`.",
